msgid "Authorization of web endpoints"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus incorporates a pluggable web security layer.\n"
"When security is active, the system performs a permission check on all HTTP "
"requests to determine if they should proceed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Authorization is based on user roles that the security provider provides.\n"
"To customize these roles, a `SecurityIdentityAugmentor` can be created, see\n"
"xref:security-customization.adoc#security-identity-customization[Security "
"Identity Customization]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Authorization using configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you work with Jakarta RESTful Web Services (JAX-RS) and need to set "
"default security requirements, consider using <<standard-security-"
"annotations>> and `quarkus.security.jaxrs.deny-unannotated-endpoints` or "
"`quarkus.security.jaxrs.default-roles-allowed` properties instead of the "
"HTTP security policy path-level matching because the security annotations "
"can override these properties on an individual JAX-RS resource or method "
"level."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Permissions are defined in the Quarkus configuration by permission sets, "
"each specifying a policy for access control."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a security policy's `paths` property contains the most specific path "
"that matches the current request path, it takes precedence over other "
"security policies with matching paths and is said to win."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configured HTTP security policy must not contain a semicolon ';' character "
"in its `paths` property.\n"
"Use <<custom-http-security-policy>> when a security policy decision depends "
"on a presence of certain matrix parameters in the request path."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Be careful with creating complex, possibly overlapping HTTP security policy "
"path expressions.\n"
"Make sure your HTTP policy configuration is thoroughly tested.\n"
"If you work with Jakarta RESTful Web Services (JAX-RS) and need to create "
"complex security policies, consider using <<standard-security-annotations>> "
"instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus policies summary"
msgstr ""

